---
// Version anglaise de /secteurs/evenementiel/. Traduction fidèle, aucune promesse ajoutée.
import ServicePage from '../../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { ZONES } from '../../../data/entite.mjs';

const zones = ZONES.map((z) => (z === 'Montréal' ? 'Montreal' : z));

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Which tasks can an event business automate?',
    a: 'Receiving requests from everywhere (email, Messenger, Instagram, website), standard estimates based on your price grid, appointment booking, deposit tracking and the thank-you email after the event with a review request.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can an AI agent reply to my clients for me?',
    a: 'Yes, according to your rules. It can answer simple questions on its own and prepare a draft for the rest. Special prices, discounts, complaints and large events always come back to you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Has FournIA worked in the events industry before?',
    a: 'Yes. For a Montreal sound equipment rental company, FournIA built the intake of its multichannel requests and an automatic follow-up after each event, with a satisfaction survey and a Google review request.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get more Google reviews after an event?',
    a: 'By asking at the right time, systematically. An email goes out after the event with a short survey: satisfied clients are directed to your Google listing, the others to you, so you can fix the problem before it becomes public.',
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  lang="en"
  alt="/secteurs/evenementiel/"
  image="/images/secteurs/evenementiel.webp"
  imageAlt="Setting up an event"
  path="/en/industries/events"
  title="Automation for event and rental businesses | FournIA"
  description="Centralized requests, fast estimates, tracked deposits and Google reviews after every event: AI automation for events and equipment rental in Quebec."
  h1="Automation for event businesses"
  lead="Requests come in by email, Messenger, Instagram and the website, often in the evening and on weekends. FournIA centralizes those requests, speeds up estimates and automates the follow-up before and after each event, for rental, sound and event planning businesses."
  serviceName="Events and rentals"
  serviceType="Process automation for event businesses"
  areaServed={zones}
  faq={faq}
  updated="2026-11-18"
>
  <h2>What costs time in the events industry</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Requests scattered</strong> across five inboxes, some of them left unanswered.</li>
    <li><strong>Estimates redone by hand</strong> for each request, even though most follow the same grid.</li>
    <li><strong>Deposits to track</strong> before each date, without forgetting anyone.</li>
    <li><strong>A forgotten after-event</strong>: no thank-you, no review request, no follow-up for next time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What FournIA can automate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A single intake</strong> for all your requests, with a first reply within minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>Standard estimates</strong> drawn from your price grid, sent after your approval.</li>
    <li><strong>Appointment booking</strong> in your real calendar for the confirmation call.</li>
    <li><strong>Deposit and invoice tracking</strong>, without chasing a client who has already paid.</li>
    <li><strong>The after-event email</strong> with a satisfaction survey and a link to your Google reviews.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>A free 30-minute discovery call.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>An assessment</strong> of the full path, from the request to the client's review.</li>
    <li><strong>The build</strong> channel by channel, starting with the one that loses the most requests.</li>
    <li><strong>Training</strong> and regular follow-up.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>See also: <a href="/en/custom-systems/">business automation</a> and the <a href="/en/industries/">other industries</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
